{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-claude/tests/wire_order_roundtrip.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:03:08.536136Z","id":"91530affc42e420098dfeeb40c3b5b719c6247c719827004baed6ef4f5e33bed","body":{"detail":"The test and the toolpath-claude CHANGELOG entry say the derived step sequence only grows as the session file does, but the test maps each step to `(s.step.id, s.step.parents)` and never compares the step bodies. conversation_to_view folds a tool-result carrier into the assistant turn that issued the tool_use (merge_tool_results_into_items in crates/toolpath-claude/src/provider.rs), so appending the carrier rewrites a step that an earlier derive already emitted. Reproduced: u1, a2 (tool_use t1 Read). Deriving that file gives step a2 with `tool_uses:[{..., name: Read}]`; appending the carrier line for t1 changes the same step to `tool_uses:[{..., result: {content: FILEBODY, is_error: false}}]`. A consumer that appends only new steps from a re-derive keeps a2 without its result forever. The behaviour is the same on origin/main; the gap is that the new test and changelog claim more than they check.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":144},"end":{"line":183},"content_hash":"be45d85ba304ab1e3033fcb048de9aa03c0700cb43c98c29032a21857f100551"},"suggested_fix":"Either compare whole serialized steps in the prefix test and decide how a late tool result is represented (for example as its own step, or by accepting that the last assistant step may be revised), or narrow the test name, doc comment and CHANGELOG wording to 'step ids and parents only grow' and state that a step's tool results can fill in later.","summary":"derived_step_sequence_is_append_only_under_file_growth compares only (id, parents), but an earlier step's body still changes when its tool result is appended","tags":["review","review:pr-144-qual-3"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-claude/tests/wire_order_roundtrip.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T14:08:45.438612Z","id":"e1ef77649048268518021bc58e2db0849c915bdd6168b1101c521f449bfec31f","body":{"detail":"derived_step_sequence_is_append_only_under_file_growth (wire_order_roundtrip.rs lines 144-183) maps steps to (s.step.id, s.step.parents) only. Temporary test on compacted_session.jsonl: deriving the first 2 lines gives step uuid-pre-2 with tool_uses [{id t-pre-1, name Read}] and no result; deriving the first 3 lines (carrier appended) gives the same step id with tool_uses[0].result = {content: \"pub fn login() { ... }\", is_error: false}; the serialized steps differ. Cause: merge_tool_results_into_items (crates/toolpath-claude/src/provider.rs line 325) writes results back into the earlier turn; main's merge_tool_results did the same. The CHANGELOG diff line 'the derived step sequence only grows as the session file does' and the test doc claim more than the test checks. Concern is the right kind.","kind":"comment","references":"91530affc42e420098dfeeb40c3b5b719c6247c719827004baed6ef4f5e33bed","summary":"confirmed: pre-existing behaviour on main, new overclaim - an already-derived assistant step's body changes when its tool result is appended","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/toolpath-claude/tests/wire_order_roundtrip.rs","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-13T20:47:25.142827Z","id":"204f798d22790158ab87e98d3fe2312876eb3a3309c76a2edefbbdf98a7fc868","body":{"detail":"Owner approval, 2026-10-13. Text written by this PR; rides along in the #144 fix pass.","kind":"decision","references":"91530affc42e420098dfeeb40c3b5b719c6247c719827004baed6ef4f5e33bed","suggested_fix":"Either compare whole serialized steps in the prefix test and decide how a late tool result is represented (for example as its own step, or by accepting that the last assistant step may be revised), or narrow the test name, doc comment and CHANGELOG wording to 'step ids and parents only grow' and state that a step's tool results can fill in later.","summary":"Decided: fix as suggested (text this PR wrote)","tags":["review:pr-144-qual-3","decision","session:claude-code:2b4a790f-c163-4549-93fa-572ef111cb5e"]}}
